{
  /* This TypeScript project config describes the environment that
   * Convex functions run in and is used to typecheck them.
   *
   * It is the one the Convex CLI generates for a new project (see
   * `tsconfigCodegen` in the CLI bundle), kept verbatim apart from the
   * comments below. This deployment went a long time without one, which meant
   * `convex codegen --typecheck` — whose default is "try, and skip silently if
   * you can't" — skipped, every time, and a deploy was the first thing that
   * ever looked at these types. On a single self-hosted deployment that means
   * a type error is found in production.
   *
   * Two settings do most of the work and are worth not "modernising":
   *
   *   lib: ES2023, NOT ESNext. TypeScript 5.7 made `Uint8Array` generic over
   *     its backing buffer (`Uint8Array<ArrayBufferLike>`), which under ESNext
   *     stops being assignable to `BufferSource` and `BodyInit`. That alone
   *     invented thirteen errors in `webPush.ts` for code that is correct and
   *     has been running in production for months. Convex's runtime is not
   *     ESNext-latest, so ES2023 is both the accurate answer and the quiet one.
   *
   *   exclude: ./_generated. Generated code is the compiler's own output and
   *     is not ours to answer for.
   */
  "compilerOptions": {
    /* These settings are not required by Convex and can be modified. */
    "allowJs": true,
    "strict": true,
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true,

    /* Empty ON PURPOSE, and not the same as omitting the field: with no
     * `types` key TypeScript pulls in every `@types/*` it can find in
     * node_modules, so installing @types/node for an unrelated tool would
     * silently change what this backend typechecks against. `process.env` —
     * the one Node-ish global in use — is declared in `env.d.ts`; see the note
     * there for why depending on @types/node was tried and rejected. */
    "types": [],

    /* These compiler options are required by Convex */
    "target": "ESNext",
    "lib": ["ES2023", "dom"],
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "module": "ESNext",
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["./**/*"],
  "exclude": ["./_generated"]
}
